--- Finding (unicode_strings): a syntax error inside a string's interpolation is
--- placed at LINE 1 of the file, at the column it has within the interpolation's
--- own text, so the message underlines the program's first line, whatever line
--- the string is on. Both modes alike (crow run -i and crow run):
---
---   unicode_strings-1.co:1:5: this ')' closes nothing — no bracket is open before it
---     1 │ --- Finding (unicode_strings): a syntax error inside a string's interpolation is
---       │     ^^^^^^^
---
--- Expected: the error placed on line 20, where the string is, under the ')'.
--- Any parse error in an interpolation does it: `log['`[1, 0x10]`']` on line 4 of
--- a program was "1:6: expected ']', got 'x10'" under line 1 (in a 90-line program
--- the message sent me to its header comment). The same text outside a string,
--- `log[[1, 0x10]]`, is placed right (4:10). Related: findings/blossom_algorithm-1.co
--- saw this position for its `match` hint; that hint is fixed, the position is not.
x = 1
log[x]
log['`x + 1`']
--- the line with the fault:
log['`x + )`']
